    <section name="What can Checkstyle check?">
      <div class="cs-grid">
        <div class="cs-card">
          <p class="cs-card-title">Naming</p>
          <p>Set conventions for types, methods, parameters, fields, and
            constants.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-card">
          <p class="cs-card-title">Imports</p>
          <p>Control star, unused, illegal, and out-of-order imports.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-card">
          <p class="cs-card-title">Javadoc</p>
          <p>Check documentation presence, structure, summaries, and
            tags.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-card">
          <p class="cs-card-title">Formatting &amp; Whitespace</p>
          <p>Enforce spacing, indentation, line wrapping, and other
            layout rules.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-card">
          <p class="cs-card-title">Class Design</p>
          <p>Check visibility, extension, utility classes, and type
            structure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-card">
          <p class="cs-card-title">Coding Practices</p>
          <p>Check declarations, control flow, common structural, and
            complexity issues.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        <a href="checks.html">View all checks →</a>
      </p>

      <div class="cs-checks-demo">
        <p class="cs-checks-demo-label">Try a few more checks:</p>

        <input type="radio" name="cs-check-demo" id="demo-starimport" class="cs-toggle-input"
               checked="checked"/>
        <input type="radio" name="cs-check-demo" id="demo-constantname" class="cs-toggle-input"/>
        <input type="radio" name="cs-check-demo" id="demo-magicnumber" class="cs-toggle-input"/>
        <input type="radio" name="cs-check-demo" id="demo-emptycatch" class="cs-toggle-input"/>
        <input type="radio" name="cs-check-demo" id="demo-methodlength" class="cs-toggle-input"/>

        <div class="cs-toggle-labels">
          <label for="demo-starimport">AvoidStarImport</label>
          <label for="demo-constantname">ConstantName</label>
          <label for="demo-magicnumber">MagicNumber</label>
          <label for="demo-emptycatch">EmptyCatchBlock</label>
          <label for="demo-methodlength">MethodLength</label>
        </div>

        <div id="panel-starimport" class="cs-toggle-panel cs-check-panel cs-code-wrapper">
          <pre class="cs-check-code">import java.util.*;</pre>
          <p class="cs-check-violation"><span class="cs-check-badge">ERROR</span>
            Test.java:1:1: Using the '.*' form of import should be avoided - java.util.*.
            <b>[AvoidStarImport]</b></p>
          <p class="cs-check-desc">Flags wildcard imports so it's always clear exactly which
            classes a file depends on.</p>
        </div>

        <div id="panel-constantname" class="cs-toggle-panel cs-check-panel cs-code-wrapper">
          <pre class="cs-check-code">public static final int maxUsers = 10;</pre>
          <p class="cs-check-violation"><span class="cs-check-badge">ERROR</span>
            Config.java:2:29: Name 'maxUsers' must match pattern
            '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]*(_[A-Z0-9]+)*$'. <b>[ConstantName]</b></p>
          <p class="cs-check-desc">Enforces SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE naming for constants, so
            they're instantly recognizable.</p>
        </div>

        <div id="panel-magicnumber" class="cs-toggle-panel cs-check-panel cs-code-wrapper">
          <pre class="cs-check-code">if (retries &gt; 3) {
  throw new RuntimeException();
}</pre>
          <p class="cs-check-violation"><span class="cs-check-badge">ERROR</span>
            Retry.java:1:15: '3' is a magic number. <b>[MagicNumber]</b></p>
          <p class="cs-check-desc">Flags unexplained numeric literals buried in logic that
            should be named constants.</p>
        </div>

        <div id="panel-emptycatch" class="cs-toggle-panel cs-check-panel cs-code-wrapper">
          <pre class="cs-check-code">try {
  process();
} catch (IOException e) {
}</pre>
          <p class="cs-check-violation"><span class="cs-check-badge">ERROR</span>
            Processor.java:3:32: Empty catch block. <b>[EmptyCatchBlock]</b></p>
          <p class="cs-check-desc">Catches silently swallowed exceptions that can hide real
            failures in production.</p>
        </div>

        <div id="panel-methodlength" class="cs-toggle-panel cs-check-panel cs-code-wrapper">
          <pre class="cs-check-code">public void handleRequest() {
  // ... 160 lines ...
}</pre>
          <p class="cs-check-violation"><span class="cs-check-badge">ERROR</span>
            Handler.java:5:3: Method length is 160 lines (max allowed is 150).
            <b>[MethodLength]</b></p>
          <p class="cs-check-desc">Flags methods that have grown too large to read, test, or
            reason about at a glance.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cs-fits-callout">
      <p class="cs-fits-title">Where Checkstyle fits</p>
      <p>
        Checkstyle focuses on configurable, source-level checks and
        processes Java files one at a time — naming, imports, Javadoc,
        formatting, and class design. It doesn't determine expression
        types or build a full inheritance hierarchy, so it's commonly
        used alongside tools that perform whole-program analysis. Read the
        <a href="writingchecks.html#Limitations">detailed limitations</a>
        for specifics.
      </p>
    </div>

